<BaseLayout title="About | Bhagyashri Patil">
<header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">About / The perspective behind the work</span><h1>Curious by nature.<br/><span class="accent">Product-minded by practice.</span></h1><p>I'm interested in the point where a real customer problem meets a thoughtful technical solution.</p></header>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">01 / My story</span><div class="content-block"><h2>More than a technology stack.</h2><p>My background is rooted in enterprise data, analytics, and solution delivery. Over time, what has interested me most is the decision-making behind the build: understanding who a solution is for, why it matters, and which trade-offs turn an idea into something genuinely useful.</p><p>That's the perspective I bring to product management, solutions engineering, and architecture opportunities. I'm comfortable moving between stakeholder conversations and technical detail, and I want to keep growing at that intersection.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Principles</span><div><h2>How I think about building.</h2></div></div><div class="cards"><article class="card"><span class="eyebrow">Discover</span><h3>Listen before solving.</h3><p>Start with users, constraints, and the business decision that needs to improve.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="eyebrow">Design</span><h3>Make trade-offs explicit.</h3><p>Balance feasibility, usability, scalability, and the value of getting an MVP into the world.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="eyebrow">Learn</span><h3>Measure and iterate.</h3><p>Define what success means and let evidence shape the next decision.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">03 / What's next</span><div><h2>Looking ahead, across industries.</h2><p>I'm exploring product-oriented and solutions engineering opportunities in Boston, Massachusetts, and remote. I'm particularly interested in data-rich products, cloud systems, and the practical application of AI—whether in technology, finance, banking, real estate, or another complex domain.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Get in touch ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="/experience/">Experience →</a></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
